@thdxr @adamdotdevin @rekram1-node @kitlangton — would appreciate a look when you have a moment.

A small TUI bug fix: model search ranks by relevance again (#50531). Since #33558 re-sorted search results by free/newest, typing `opus` pre-selects `MiMo-V2.6-Pro-UltraSpeed` over `Claude Opus 5`. Search now keeps fuzzysort's order; the unfiltered list keeps the existing sort.

Tests added in `model-options.test.ts`; typecheck, oxlint and prettier clean locally. (The dialog maximize change that was here is now separate, pending design direction on #47600.)

@thdxr @adamdotdevin @rekram1-node @kitlangton — would appreciate a look when you have a moment.

`opencode models --verbose` currently dumps raw JSON (1,242 lines for Anthropic alone). This prints one aligned table per provider instead: id, name, cost per 1M tokens, context/output limits, capabilities. Plain `opencode models` output is unchanged byte for byte so scripts piping it into `grep`/`fzf` keep working, and the table is colourless on stdout so it survives redirects.

Closes #50513, with tests in `models.test.ts` and the CLI docs updated. Happy to change anything.

@ZipiDan thanks for testing this and for the Podman repro. I looked at both closed PRs before deciding what to do here:

- #38992 fixes the same thing in the same place as this PR (it seeds the browser's open-projects list). It had two guards this PR lacked, so I've added them, crediting #38992: the server folder is only adopted when no project is open yet, and a folder you closed stays closed (before this, it came back on every reload). There are unit tests for both.
- I've left #35976 out on purpose. The server already reports its working directory to the web app, so in your `--workdir /workspace` case this PR registers `/workspace` without `--dir`. The `/` you see in `GET /project` is the shared `global` project that every non-git folder uses. #35976 would set that shared record's worktree to whichever non-git folder was opened last, and several folders would then overwrite each other. That may still be worth changing, but it's a design decision for the maintainers and better handled in its own issue than bundled into this fix.

Also, contributors can't reopen PRs someone else closed. That's up to the maintainers or the original authors.

@Hona @Brendonovich (CODEOWNERS for `packages/app`): could one of you take a look when you have a moment? It's a small change (3 files in `packages/app/src/context`, with tests) and it fixes the empty web UI on a fresh `opencode web`/`serve` (#37096, and the sidebar part of #39655).
